ases.\"},{\"loc\":\"note\",\"q\":\"Each submitting laboratory source was considered a primary sampling unit, and the state and week of sequence specimen collection were considered strata.\"}]},{\"name\":\"suppression of regional estimates with <300 sequences\",\"class\":\"transformation\",\"regression_family\":null,\"inferred_from\":\"small-sample suppression rule for HHS regional proportions\",\"role\":\"ancillary\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"note\",\"q\":\"variant proportions from HHS regions with fewer than 300 sequences in a 2-week period are not reported on CDC’s COVID Data Tracker\"}]}],\"comparison\":{\"framework\":\"group\",\"scale\":null,\"referent\":\"prevalence thresholds of >10% and >50% (predominance)\",\"across\":[\"lineage group\",\"2-week period\",\"HHS region\"],\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"text\",\"q\":\"None of these XBB lineage groups attained predominance (>50% prevalence), but five groups reached a prevalence of ≥10%.\"}]},\"inference\":{\"v\":\"none\",\"method_stated\":false,\"ev\":[]},\"primary_measures\":[{\"v\":\"variant proportion (prevalence, %)\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"figure 1\",\"q\":\"National estimates of biweekly proportions* of SARS-CoV-2 variants\"}]},{\"v\":\"normalized frequency of variant-attributed COVID-19 cases\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"figure 1\",\"q\":\"estimated normalized frequency of variant-attributed COVID-19 cases\"}]},{\"v\":\"number of spike protein amino acid differences\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"figure 2\",\"q\":\"number of spike protein amino acid differences (including substitutions, insertions, and deletions) relative to Wuhan-Hu-1 reference\"}]}],\"regression_fields\":null,\"public_health_question\":{\"v\":\"Which SARS-CoV-2 lineages circulated in the United States during May 2023–September 2024, and how did their proportions change over time?\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"summary\",\"q\":\"This report summarizes U.S. trends in variant proportion estimates during May 2023–September 2024\"}]},\"conditions\":[{\"v\":\"COVID-19\",\"role\":\"outcome\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"title\",\"q\":\"Genomic Surveillance for SARS-CoV-2 Variants: Circulation of Omicron XBB and JN.1 Lineages\"}]}],\"study_design\":[{\"v\":\"surveillance/descriptive\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"summary\",\"q\":\"CDC continues to track the evolution of SARS-CoV-2, including the Omicron variant and its descendants, using national genomic surveillance.\"}]},{\"v\":\"before/after or trend\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"summary\",\"q\":\"This report summarizes U.S. trends in variant proportion estimates during May 2023–September 2024\"}]}],\"data_source_type\":[{\"v\":\"CDC surveillance system\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"text\",\"q\":\"CDC integrates SARS-CoV-2 sequence data from 1) the National SARS-CoV-2 Strain Surveillance (NS3) program\"},{\"loc\":\"text\",\"q\":\"was the primary data source for survey weights beginning November 17, 2023.\"}]},{\"v\":\"other\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"text\",\"q\":\"2) CDC-contracted commercial laboratories, and 3) public sequence data repositories.\"},{\"loc\":\"note\",\"q\":\"Public sequence data repositories included the Global Initiative on Sharing All Influenza Data and National Center for Biotechnology Information GenBank databases.\"}]}],\"data_source_named\":[{\"v\":\"National SARS-CoV-2 Strain Surveillance (NS3)\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"text\",\"q\":\"the National SARS-CoV-2 Strain Surveillance (NS3) program\"}]},{\"v\":\"National Respiratory and Enteric Virus Surveillance System (NREVSS)\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"text\",\"q\":\"The National Respiratory and Enteric Virus Surveillance System (NREVSS)\"}]},{\"v\":\"GISAID\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"note\",\"q\":\"Global Initiative on Sharing All Influenza Data\"}]},{\"v\":\"NCBI GenBank\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"note\",\"q\":\"National Center for Biotechnology Information GenBank databases\"}]},{\"v\":\"COVID-19 electronic laboratory reporting (CELR)\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"note\",\"q\":\"the number of positive specimens by HHS region was obtained from COVID-19 electronic laboratory reporting (CELR)\"}]}],\"setting\":{\"v\":\"US national\",\"ev\":[{\"loc\":\"text\",\"q\":\"A total of 208,357 SARS-CoV-2 sequences from 56 U.S. jurisdictions\"}]},\"vaccine_outcome_type\":null,\"equity\":{\"level\":0,\"level_reason\":\"Results are by lineage, period and HHS region only; no social-position dimension is defined, analyzed or discussed.\",\"level_confidence\":\"high\",\"level_alternative\":null,\"dimensions\":[],\"determinants_of_health\":{\"v\":null,\"ev\":[]},\"equity_action\":{\"v\":false,\"ev\":[]},\"equity_measurement\":null},\"groupwise\":[],\"uncertain_fields\":[\"outcome_types\",\"procedures\"],\"confidence\":\"high\",\"notes\":\"The multinomial-regression Nowcast is excluded from this analysis (data limited to sequences older than 4 weeks), so it is not recorded as a procedure. Normalized case frequency is arithmetic (counts × proportions scaled to the maximum), and the 5,000-sequence subsample for Figure 2 is a sampling step. Sensitivity analyses in Limitations are cited from an earlier report.\",\"view_issues\":\"Figure 2 description says 'S1 domain substitutions' and January 2021–August 2024, whereas its title says amino acid differences through September 14, 2024. Text typo 'JN.1was'. article.txt table rows omit reference residues 450 and 481 (N) shown in the CSV.\"}", "type": "text"}]}